ivider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T14:27:41-07:00","id":1339062,"title":"","content":"I, for one, welcome our new Dragon King overlords.<br /> <br /> More seriously, this sounds like an interesting book. While the idea of how dragons might fit in to a world full of gods gives a lot to play with, I'm mainly eager to see how this works as a sort of stand alone thing where dragons go out into the world and do dragony things in a suitably epic fashion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T15:37:41-07:00","id":1339072,"title":"","content":"I didn't saw the timestamp and wasn't my intention to be aggressive, I think I failed a perception roll (oh, we don't have perception rolls in Scion 2e). I think it will be awesome the idea of dragons and even we could have a scenario similar &quot;in spirit&quot; to Fireborn RPG.<br /> <br /> Now I want badly to see what types of &quot;purviews&quot; or similar rules Dragons will have because I want to use them as antagonists :v","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23839-oxcelot","name":"Oxcelot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T18:37:31-08:00","id":1372071,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the necromancy but I do want to ask, these Kick starters got delayed and I didn't miss them?<br /> I'm eagerly awaiting Dragon. What can I say I love the idea. There are many myths about dragons from them being dumb beasts to beings with power equal to a titan, to even being beings who can make Pantheons respond with &quot;Oh Shit It's Awake!&quot;, gives me a happy feeling and a desire to include Dragon Scions in my game both as antagonists and as player characters. So please don't tell me I missed my shot to back this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T18:42:30-08:00","id":1372072,"title":"","content":"There have been no Kickstarters for Dragon or Mythos. As far as I know,